.TH COOL-S 6 "2025" "cool-s 1.0.0" "Games"
.SH NAME
cool-s \- draw the legendary Cool S in your terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cool-s
[\fB-f\fR]
[\fB-d\fR \fIUSECS\fR]
[\fB-s\fR \fISCALE\fR]
[\fB-r\fR]
[\fB--no-sparks\fR]
[\fB--plain\fR]
[\fB-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cool-s
animates the step-by-step construction of the \fICool S\fR (also known as
the Universal S, Super S, Pointy S, or Graffiti S) — the ubiquitous
graffiti symbol that every school-aged child in the late 20th century
doodled on notebooks and desks.

The symbol consists of 14 line segments drawn in seven stages,
each rendered in a distinct color as the shape is assembled before your eyes.
Spark particles fly from the tip of each segment as it is drawn.
After construction, the shape flashes to a final solid white.

The program is inspired by
.BR sl (1)
(steam locomotive) and shares the same philosophy: a tiny piece of
terminal whimsy that makes you smile.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -f
Fast mode. Skip animation and render the final Cool S instantly.
.TP
.BI -d " USECS"
Set the per-pixel draw delay in microseconds. Lower values are faster;
0 is equivalent to
.BR -f .
Default: 25000 (25 ms).
.TP
.BI -s " SCALE"
Set the scale factor, 1–8. The height of the Cool S in terminal rows is
approximately \fI5 × SCALE\fR. Default: 4.
.TP
.B -r
Rainbow finale mode. After construction, the symbol cycles through all
stage colors before settling on white.
.TP
.B --no-sparks
Disable the spark particle effect.
.TP
.B --plain
Disable all ANSI color and bold formatting. Useful for redirecting output
or for terminals that do not support color.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Animate at default scale:
.IP
.B cool-s
.PP
Render a large Cool S instantly:
.IP
.B cool-s -f -s 6
.PP
Slow cinematic draw with rainbow finale:
.IP
.B cool-s -d 60000 -r
.PP
Small, colorless:
.IP
.B cool-s -s 2 --plain
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
0
Normal exit (or user pressed a key to dismiss).
.TP
1
Invalid command-line option.
.SH HISTORY
The Cool S (also "Universal S") is a piece of childlore whose origin is
unknown but dates at least to the early 1980s. It consists of exactly
14 line segments — six short vertical bars in two groups of three,
two diagonal connectors, a top inverted-V, a bottom V, and two closing
horizontal connectors — forming a stylized, pointy S shape.
.PP
.B cool-s
was written as a tribute to that tiny act of creativity every kid
performed with a ballpoint pen. Now your terminal can do it too.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR sl (1),
.BR fortune (6),
.BR figlet (6)
